# Release trees are hash-verified: every release ships a sha256sums.txt and a
# registry that pins each cartridge and payload by SHA-256.
#
# Git's default eol conversion rewrites LF to CRLF on Windows checkout, which
# changes the bytes and therefore every one of those hashes. Measured on
# 202608300309-pipelinenews: all four cartridge and payload digests failed on a
# Windows checkout, and all four matched again once the CRs were stripped.
# The hashes were correct; the checkout was not.
#
# Treating release trees as binary keeps the bytes identical everywhere, so a
# release verifies on the machine that built it and on the machine that reads it.
releases/** -text
